            <categoryCaption>Control</categoryCaption>
            <categoryName>Control</categoryName>
            <hidden>false</hidden>
            <onlineHelp>Allows to specify how to distribute 
extra space. If the layout is smaller 
than the area it needs to fill, the 
extra space is distributed to each 
field control in proportion to its 
specified vertical/horizontal weight. 
A control that has a weight of zero 
receives no extra space. If all the 
weights are zero, all the extra space 
appears between the grids of the 
cell and the edges. The weight should
be non-negative. The cell occupation
mode determines whether to resize 
the component to fill its display area, 
and if so, how.</onlineHelp>
            <customFieldCaption>Display Area</customFieldCaption>
            <displayedAsSingletonList>false</displayedAsSingletonList>
            <duplicateGenerated>false</duplicateGenerated>
