        <fieldsCustomization>
            <uniqueIdentifier>5cf35c3:1980891bae2:446f</uniqueIdentifier>
            <specificProperties/>
            <hidden>false</hidden>
            <onlineHelp>If this option is disabled, active validity value checking
will result in validation attempts for all elements in the 
list (or tree), potentially creating an infinite loop with 
tree nodes having infinite number of descendants.
However, if this option is enabled, the specified field
will be used to check, for each element, whether its 
validity should be checked or not (if the field value is 
true, the element will be validated; otherwise, the 
element and its entire subtree will not be validated).
Note that if the specified field name does not match 
any field for one of the existing elements, an error will 
be raised. If multiple fields match the specification, 
then only the first one will be considered.</onlineHelp>
            <customFieldCaption>Validation Enablement Status Field Name</customFieldCaption>
            <displayedAsSingletonList>false</displayedAsSingletonList>
            <duplicateGenerated>false</duplicateGenerated>
            <fieldName>itemValidabilityStatusFieldNamePattern</fieldName>
